Description: Thread-safe C++ trust region optimizers, each exposed
    both as an R function and as a C-callable entry point (with function
    pointers registered for other packages to call without linking
    against this package's shared library) so they can be used from
    parallel C++ code such as in 'nlmixr2est'. Includes a port of the
    two-derivative trust region algorithm in the 'trust' package by
    Charles J. Geyer; a port of the Steihaug truncated conjugate-gradient
    trust region method from the 'basin' Rust crate (Steihaug (1983)
    <doi:10.1137/0720042>); and ports of M. J. D. Powell's
    derivative-free BOBYQA and NEWUOA methods as distributed in the
    'minqa' package.
